repository-code: "https://github.com/SIGALT/Reef-Analytics"
url: "https://sigalt.github.io/Reef-Analytics/"

abstract: >
  Reef Analytics is an open scientific software platform for exploring,
  quantifying, and comparing coral colony architecture and three-dimensional
  structural complexity. The current alpha version integrates synthetic coral
  geometry, interactive 3D visualization, morphometric metrics, three-dimensional
  fractal dimension estimation, surface area, colony volume, projected area,
  colony height, shelter volume, and T0-T1 comparisons. The project is being
  developed toward the integration and analysis of empirical 3D coral models
  derived from photogrammetry, scanning, and other three-dimensional
  reconstruction techniques.

keywords:
  - coral reefs
  - coral morphology
  - coral architecture
  - 3D models
  - photogrammetry
  - structure from motion
  - Gaussian splatting
  - fractal dimension
  - structural complexity
  - shelter volume
  - marine ecology
